      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Stop that immediately, butter and tea tree oil are absolute no-nos that will trap heat and introduce bacteria, making your burn worse and more likely to get infected. You need to cool the area under running tap water for at least 20 minutes right now to stop the burning and reduce swelling. Once cooled, apply a thick layer of plain petroleum jelly and cover it with a sterile non-stick bandage to protect the blisters from popping. Do not pop any blisters yourself, and if the pain becomes unbearable or the skin turns black, you must go to the ER immediately.",
